WEBVTT

00:01.950 --> 00:11.820
While watching anime, make sure not to sit too close to the screen and that the room is well lit.

00:10.140 --> 00:16.440
After the fierce fight against the Flare Gang, Satoshi and his friends have been working diligently towards the reopening of the Miare Gym.

00:20.260 --> 00:21.690
Okay, you can stop now.

00:22.640 --> 00:23.950
Thank you, Pikachu.

00:26.480 --> 00:26.950
All right,

00:27.300 --> 00:28.130
let's take a break.

00:28.660 --> 00:29.800
Thank you very much.

00:30.430 --> 00:31.930
How's your injury doing?

00:32.470 --> 00:33.380
I'm fine.

00:33.780 --> 00:36.300
After all, I'm more fit than the average person!

00:37.480 --> 00:38.820
We're almost there.

00:39.120 --> 00:39.600
Yeah.

00:39.920 --> 00:41.560
All that's left is a final check.

00:42.200 --> 00:43.520
It should be usable by tomorrow.

00:44.180 --> 00:45.770
All right, all right!

00:46.360 --> 00:47.950
I'm sure Citron will be happy.

00:53.120 --> 00:53.920
Okay then...

00:54.340 --> 00:55.610
How is this?

00:59.840 --> 01:00.440
Activated.

01:00.810 --> 01:01.080
Activated.

01:01.860 --> 01:03.330
I am the Citroid.

01:03.760 --> 01:04.730
Nice to meet you.

01:07.420 --> 01:09.030
I am your master, Citron.

01:10.120 --> 01:10.520
Nice to meet you,

01:10.880 --> 01:11.410
Citroid.

01:12.370 --> 01:13.670
Citron... sama.

01:16.710 --> 01:17.220
Yeah.

01:17.810 --> 01:21.220
We have already received information on the destruction of the Flare Gang.

01:21.650 --> 01:23.440
It hasn't been made public, but...

01:23.840 --> 01:29.100
It was <i>our</i> successful plan that led to the Flare Gang's destruction.

01:29.540 --> 01:31.860
Oh? I'd like a detailed report on that.

01:32.090 --> 01:32.400
Roger!

01:32.870 --> 01:37.320
As soon as the Miare Airport reopens, we'll return to headquarters.

01:37.760 --> 01:38.060
Good.

01:38.830 --> 01:40.110
I'm looking forward to it.

01:43.070 --> 01:44.260
You heard that?

01:44.560 --> 01:46.730
We've been rewarded for our hard work!

01:47.100 --> 01:50.080
Us working ourselves to death on Kalosian land has paid off!

01:50.800 --> 01:51.840
All right!

01:52.170 --> 01:53.630
Hooray!

01:54.490 --> 01:56.130
Uh, but something's missing.

01:56.560 --> 01:56.980
Huh?

01:57.250 --> 02:00.080
A surprise that'll make Sakaki-sama speechless!

02:00.560 --> 02:01.430
That's right!

02:01.770 --> 02:04.360
If we bring the brat boy's Pikachu back with us as a souvenir,

02:04.570 --> 02:06.890
Sakaki-sama will be speechless <i>and</i> all smiles!

02:07.570 --> 02:09.900
There's no doubt we'll be promoted.

02:10.570 --> 02:12.460
This feels good!

02:19.230 --> 02:24.910
We Start at Zero!
Citron's Decision!!

02:26.070 --> 02:26.650
I see.

02:27.430 --> 02:28.260
So it hasn't returned.

02:28.870 --> 02:29.570
No way!

02:28.950 --> 02:38.820
Play a board game via the Pocket Monsters XY& data broadcast!
Press the d-button on your remote and try reaching the battles and the presents!!

02:28.950 --> 02:38.820
Z

02:31.650 --> 02:33.410
You cannot recover...

02:34.030 --> 02:35.550
...what has been erased entirely.

02:36.900 --> 02:38.820
Uhm, excuse me.

02:39.990 --> 02:41.840
I've come to challenge the Miare Gym.

02:44.630 --> 02:45.630
You're Satoshi!

02:46.070 --> 02:46.550
Huh?

02:47.230 --> 02:49.600
The Kalos League finals were awesome!

02:50.200 --> 02:51.310
You watched it, huh?

02:51.790 --> 02:53.690
It was incredibly cool!

02:53.690 --> 02:55.060
I got so fired up!

02:55.330 --> 02:57.850
That's why I want to enter the League too, no matter what!

02:58.250 --> 02:59.240
You want a Gym match, correct?

02:59.830 --> 03:02.150
I am Citron, the Gym Leader of the Miare Gym.

03:02.540 --> 03:02.790
Uh...

03:03.690 --> 03:03.990
Huh?

03:04.630 --> 03:05.450
Uhm...

03:05.840 --> 03:06.770
Where's the Citroid?

03:08.850 --> 03:10.080
...And that is the story.

03:10.690 --> 03:11.790
I see...

03:12.500 --> 03:14.920
I challenged the Gym the other day,

03:15.400 --> 03:17.600
but I got beaten to a pulp by the Citroid.

03:17.870 --> 03:18.220
What?

03:19.110 --> 03:20.850
I was so frustrated...

03:21.510 --> 03:23.590
That's why I want to fight the Citroid one more time...

03:23.950 --> 03:25.010
...and get the badge!

03:25.670 --> 03:27.750
I've been training with that in mind!

03:28.260 --> 03:29.720
I get that feeling!

03:30.650 --> 03:33.780
Having a goal is what motivates a Trainer and their Pokémon to do their best!

03:35.810 --> 03:37.350
What will you do, bro?

03:40.510 --> 03:41.990
It can battle, but...

03:42.420 --> 03:43.670
...it has been reset, so...

03:43.950 --> 03:46.380
...it has no recollection of ever battling you.

03:47.350 --> 03:49.370
I want to fight the Citroid.

03:50.070 --> 03:50.850
Please!

03:52.950 --> 03:53.840
I got it.

03:55.160 --> 03:55.450
But...

03:55.950 --> 03:58.120
...seeing as how the battlefield is not even ready yet,

03:58.610 --> 04:00.130
could you come back tomorrow?

04:01.430 --> 04:03.460
I will do what I can to adjust the Citroid.

04:04.620 --> 04:05.110
Okay!

04:07.860 --> 04:08.940
Thank you very much!

04:10.830 --> 04:11.590
See you tomorrow!

04:12.130 --> 04:13.250
See you!

04:13.980 --> 04:14.900
Hey, Satoshi-kun!

04:15.350 --> 04:16.930
Professor Platane called.

04:17.490 --> 04:19.440
He said Alan's coming back today.

04:20.040 --> 04:20.730
Is Alan?

04:27.160 --> 04:28.930
Ow...

04:32.560 --> 04:33.490
Hello!

04:34.470 --> 04:36.420
Oh, Satoshi! Guys!

04:36.690 --> 04:37.780
What happened, Manon?

04:38.560 --> 04:39.540
Just a little...

04:40.400 --> 04:41.160
Is this...?

04:41.580 --> 04:44.770
Since Alan's coming back, I thought I could throw him a little party.

04:47.750 --> 04:49.630
It kind of smells like something has burned...

04:50.320 --> 04:51.060
Oh no!

04:52.660 --> 04:55.590
I worked so hard on this special main course and yet...

04:57.350 --> 04:57.980
Oh, right!

04:58.310 --> 05:00.350
Manon, do you still have ingredients left?

05:01.700 --> 05:03.660
With a bit of creativity we can do something about this.

05:04.280 --> 05:05.230
I'll help you.

05:05.740 --> 05:06.910
I will help as well.

05:07.310 --> 05:09.080
If we all work together, we'll still make it in time!

05:10.460 --> 05:12.240
Eureka will decorate, then!

05:13.560 --> 05:15.100
Thanks, everyone!

05:18.510 --> 05:19.170
Thanks for the good work.

05:19.530 --> 05:20.600
It must've been hard for you, right?

05:21.340 --> 05:21.690
No.

05:39.110 --> 05:41.160
I wonder what Squishy is up to...

05:48.070 --> 05:49.360
I'm sure it's doing all right.

05:51.990 --> 05:52.780
You're right.

05:53.410 --> 05:55.200
It must be sunbathing somewhere.

05:57.860 --> 05:59.780
Ta-da! It's done!

06:00.390 --> 06:01.350
Looks great!

06:03.490 --> 06:03.970
We're back!

06:05.180 --> 06:05.830
Professor!

06:06.330 --> 06:06.590
Come on.

06:13.180 --> 06:13.880
Welcome back!

06:14.680 --> 06:18.650
Alan... You see, today we're throwing a party to celebrate your return. We've arranged this together!

06:18.650 --> 06:19.770
We've been waiting for you, Alan!

06:21.220 --> 06:23.160
Come on, let's eat before it gets cold!

06:23.630 --> 06:24.890
I will pour the tea now.

06:26.950 --> 06:27.690
Isn't this nice?

06:32.940 --> 06:35.000
This is quite well done.

06:35.690 --> 06:36.620
Isn't it tasty?

06:54.030 --> 06:55.680
Alan, try this!

06:59.110 --> 06:59.530
What do you think?

06:59.980 --> 07:00.680
Is it good?

07:01.550 --> 07:01.740
Yeah.

07:02.400 --> 07:03.680
That's great!

07:04.270 --> 07:06.190
So the Miare Gym is also finally reopening, huh?

07:06.420 --> 07:08.290
A challenger is going to come right away!

07:08.600 --> 07:08.840
Right?

07:09.020 --> 07:10.020
Y-Yes...

07:10.760 --> 07:12.470
What will you guys do now?

07:12.710 --> 07:14.070
Uh... I...

07:14.070 --> 07:16.070
I'm thinking of going back to Kanto.

07:16.640 --> 07:18.280
I'll return to Masara Town and start over from square one...

07:18.540 --> 07:20.800
No, from <i>zero</i>.

07:22.550 --> 07:23.240
From zero?

07:23.670 --> 07:24.000
Yes.

07:24.560 --> 07:26.290
There are still so many strong Trainers out there.

07:27.050 --> 07:28.230
So I'll start my training all over again.

07:28.420 --> 07:30.590
Ah, that's so like you, Satoshi-kun.

07:36.500 --> 07:37.240
Harimaron?!

07:37.740 --> 07:39.050
You've overeaten <i>again</i>?!

07:39.830 --> 07:40.680
Let's carry it to a bed.

07:40.060 --> 07:41.620
Geez... It is hopeless.

07:42.390 --> 07:43.170
Come on, this way.

07:54.200 --> 07:55.030
You look well.

07:56.880 --> 07:58.620
You haven't seen them in a long time, have you?

08:01.640 --> 08:01.930
No.

08:03.410 --> 08:05.940
Alan, have you decided what you're going to do now?

08:07.590 --> 08:08.660
I don't know yet.

08:09.980 --> 08:10.540
I see.

08:12.190 --> 08:14.950
I may not have known the director's actual intentions,

08:15.950 --> 08:16.920
but I did help him...

08:17.690 --> 08:17.910
Huh?

08:18.630 --> 08:20.740
I've caused trouble for many people and Pokémon...

08:21.560 --> 08:23.490
...and made mistakes I can't atone for.

08:24.660 --> 08:25.060
Alan...

08:26.770 --> 08:27.590
I don't know...

08:27.890 --> 08:28.630
...what I should do.

08:30.680 --> 08:32.700
You see, I don't really get it,

08:35.740 --> 08:37.990
but I know I had fun when I battled you.

08:39.690 --> 08:40.390
During the finals...

08:40.840 --> 08:42.330
...I was so excited and thrilled.

08:44.400 --> 08:46.830
I'm sure my Pokémon felt the same way.

08:47.700 --> 08:48.350
Satoshi...

08:49.400 --> 08:49.950
That's why...

08:50.660 --> 08:51.250
Well...

08:51.790 --> 08:53.010
Let's just decide this:

08:53.980 --> 08:55.180
You and I will battle again some day. Okay?

08:57.110 --> 08:57.310
Huh?

08:58.150 --> 08:58.760
Nothing.

08:59.980 --> 09:02.040
You've always helped me.

09:02.660 --> 09:03.490
This time is no different...

09:04.480 --> 09:05.780
I just can't outdo you.

09:07.360 --> 09:08.110
Yeah.

09:08.590 --> 09:09.510
Let's battle again.

09:13.980 --> 09:14.730
Pikachu!

09:16.150 --> 09:17.320
Pokémon Quiz.

09:17.620 --> 09:18.300
The answer is...?

09:18.510 --> 09:19.350
The answer is...?!

09:20.950 --> 09:30.930
Coming up next:

09:20.950 --> 09:25.920
The Rocket Gang VS Satoshi & Alan!!

09:21.910 --> 09:26.580
Pocket Monsters XY&Z is brought to you by these sponsors.

09:25.990 --> 09:30.930
How will the Citroid's battle go!?

09:37.520 --> 09:38.230
What happened?

09:38.710 --> 09:39.800
They took Pikachu!

09:46.050 --> 09:47.640
Rocket Gang! You guys again?!

09:48.000 --> 09:50.280
If you ask us "You guys again?!",

09:50.620 --> 09:52.640
It is the world's mercy that makes us answer!

09:53.070 --> 09:55.150
To prevent the world's destruction!

09:55.410 --> 09:57.510
To protect the world's peace!

09:57.930 --> 10:00.520
Carrying out the evil of love and truth,

10:01.250 --> 10:03.660
we're lovely, charmy villains!

10:04.700 --> 10:05.360
Musashi!

10:05.700 --> 10:06.200
Kojiro!

10:06.670 --> 10:09.320
For the Rocket Gang duo dashing across the galaxy,

10:09.650 --> 10:12.160
a white hole, a white tomorrow awaits ahead!

10:12.330 --> 10:13.990
Just kidding!

10:17.990 --> 10:19.880
You guys shall release Pikachu!

10:20.440 --> 10:24.920
"Shall release"? <i>You</i> shall stop giving us orders with that condescending attitude!

10:25.120 --> 10:28.380
You see, this Pikachu will be our souvenir as we make our triumphant return to Kanto!

10:30.360 --> 10:31.490
We won't let you do this!

10:31.750 --> 10:33.290
Gekkouga, Water Shuriken!

10:36.070 --> 10:37.510
Pumpjin, Shadow Ball!

10:37.670 --> 10:39.160
Maaiika, Psybeam!

10:44.860 --> 10:46.070
Use Seed Bomb next!

10:47.470 --> 10:47.930
Lizardon,

10:48.320 --> 10:49.210
Flamethrower!

10:54.750 --> 10:56.500
Argh, let's get them too!

10:56.700 --> 10:58.290
Nyarth, use full power and suck them in.

10:58.500 --> 10:58.880
Sure!

11:00.880 --> 11:03.550
Gekkouga, use Cut to destroy that device!

11:08.870 --> 11:10.060
Pikachu, are you all right?

11:11.830 --> 11:13.350
Now you've done it!

11:13.430 --> 11:14.470
Dark Pulse!

11:13.430 --> 11:14.470
Psybeam!

11:15.490 --> 11:16.630
Tairenar, Flamethrower!

11:17.750 --> 11:18.980
Harimaron, Pin Missile!

11:22.510 --> 11:24.010
Pikachu, Thunderbolt!

11:26.770 --> 11:28.180
Lizardon, Flamethrower!

11:32.000 --> 11:36.690
Come to think about it, those two <i>did </i>make it to the finals of the Kalos League...

11:36.690 --> 11:39.510
With those two as our opponents, the odds were against us.

11:40.110 --> 11:42.110
I won't give up on that souvenir, no matter what!

11:42.630 --> 11:44.540
Next time we'll get Pikachu for sure!

11:45.190 --> 11:47.200
This feels bad!

11:52.040 --> 11:53.640
You really are amazing, Alan.

11:54.320 --> 11:55.390
So are you, Satoshi.

11:56.630 --> 11:57.510
Well then,

11:58.450 --> 11:59.770
let's repair this again.

12:05.390 --> 12:05.820
All right,

12:06.320 --> 12:07.380
Today will be your first battle.

12:08.550 --> 12:09.430
Let us do this with enthusiasm.

12:11.570 --> 12:17.870
The Miare Gym match between deputy Gym Leader Citroid and challenger Alba will now begin.

12:18.920 --> 12:20.400
You may both use three Pokémon each.

12:21.230 --> 12:25.090
As soon as one party's Pokémon are all unable to battle, the battle is over.

12:25.970 --> 12:27.430
Citroid, here we go.

12:27.980 --> 12:29.920
Yes. My first one is Coil.

12:32.920 --> 12:34.380
Vivillon, today we'll win!

12:37.380 --> 12:40.020
I'm looking forward to seeing what kind of battle this will turn out to be.

12:41.400 --> 12:42.180
Now then...

12:42.510 --> 12:43.150
Begin!

12:46.390 --> 12:47.100
Vivillon...

12:47.100 --> 12:48.330
A Bug/Flying type.

12:48.330 --> 12:49.450
Its weakness is Electric.

12:50.180 --> 12:51.300
Electro Ball!

12:53.110 --> 12:53.600
Vivillon,

12:53.880 --> 12:54.560
Flash!

12:57.330 --> 12:57.630
What?

12:58.130 --> 12:58.620
Quiver Dance!

13:03.430 --> 13:03.970
Next...

13:04.230 --> 13:04.670
Next...

13:04.670 --> 13:05.130
Calm down!

13:05.800 --> 13:06.820
Observe it carefully.

13:07.350 --> 13:09.800
Predict its movements and command an attack!

13:10.420 --> 13:11.250
Observe?

13:11.470 --> 13:12.180
Predict?

13:12.880 --> 13:13.550
Vivillon,

13:13.720 --> 13:14.350
Sleep Powder!

13:17.490 --> 13:17.990
Now!

13:17.990 --> 13:18.890
Use Energy Ball!

13:23.350 --> 13:23.850
Coil!

13:25.920 --> 13:27.320
Coil is unable to battle.

13:27.320 --> 13:28.400
Vivillon wins!

13:28.800 --> 13:29.330
All right!

13:30.000 --> 13:32.670
He rendered the opponent completely immobile with Sleep Powder!

13:33.030 --> 13:34.800
Then he instantly used that moment to fire.

13:35.150 --> 13:36.000
He's good!

13:37.110 --> 13:38.230
Please return.

13:39.460 --> 13:40.480
Listen, Citroid.

13:40.900 --> 13:42.340
You must not get agitated!

13:42.980 --> 13:44.130
Watch your opponent closely.

13:44.720 --> 13:45.090
Okay.

13:45.710 --> 13:46.870
I will not lose this time.

13:47.660 --> 13:48.470
Rarecoil!

13:49.830 --> 13:51.420
Vivillon, Sleep Powder!

13:52.640 --> 13:53.360
Rain Dance!

14:00.850 --> 14:02.220
Rarecoil, Thunder!

14:06.410 --> 14:07.000
Vivillon!

14:09.630 --> 14:10.490
Vivillon is unable to battle!

14:10.890 --> 14:11.950
Rarecoil wins!

14:13.080 --> 14:16.030
You used Rain Dance to restrain its movements and then attacked with Thunder.

14:16.600 --> 14:17.740
That was well thought out.

14:19.110 --> 14:19.450
Yes!

14:19.860 --> 14:22.660
I made a plan based on observation and prediction!

14:22.880 --> 14:23.960
I will win the next fight, too.

14:24.540 --> 14:25.390
Flamethrower!

14:26.050 --> 14:26.560
Thunder!

14:29.690 --> 14:30.760
Kaenjishi is unable to battle!

14:31.220 --> 14:32.530
Rarecoil wins!

14:33.050 --> 14:33.960
We did it!

14:34.230 --> 14:34.850
What do you think?

14:35.280 --> 14:36.390
Winning makes you happy, does it not?

14:36.900 --> 14:37.330
Yes.

14:38.180 --> 14:39.250
This is my last one.

14:39.670 --> 14:40.950
I'm counting on you, Karakara!

14:43.620 --> 14:44.240
Karakara...

14:44.560 --> 14:45.520
A Ground type.

14:45.760 --> 14:47.170
Electric moves will have no effect.

14:47.590 --> 14:48.540
Its weakness is Water.

14:49.010 --> 14:50.610
Rarecoil is at a disadvantage.

14:50.830 --> 14:51.370
Karakara,

14:51.660 --> 14:52.600
Bonemerang!

14:55.050 --> 14:56.740
Rarecoil, Sonic Boom!

14:58.890 --> 15:00.240
Go, Brick Break!

15:07.940 --> 15:09.470
Rarecoil is unable to battle!

15:09.850 --> 15:11.000
Karakara wins!

15:12.510 --> 15:13.110
All right!

15:14.870 --> 15:16.850
Rarecoil, please return.

15:18.210 --> 15:19.350
Losing is frustrating.

15:20.550 --> 15:22.710
But that is a component that makes you stronger...

15:23.710 --> 15:24.670
...and what will enable you to be better next time.

15:25.430 --> 15:26.730
The battle is not over yet.

15:27.230 --> 15:27.770
Yes.

15:28.390 --> 15:29.980
Please come out, Elezard!

15:30.270 --> 15:31.110
I am counting on you!

15:34.700 --> 15:36.500
I will get my badge for sure!

15:36.910 --> 15:38.470
Karakara, Brick Break!

15:39.140 --> 15:40.390
Dodge, Elezard!

15:43.650 --> 15:45.030
I cannot use Electric moves.

15:45.270 --> 15:45.970
So in that case...

15:46.480 --> 15:47.140
Dragon Tail!

15:50.180 --> 15:50.510
Guard yourself!

15:54.250 --> 15:55.350
Bone Rush!

15:57.830 --> 15:58.470
Focus Blast!

16:04.120 --> 16:04.770
How is that?

16:07.780 --> 16:08.060
All right.

16:08.950 --> 16:10.200
We won't give up.

16:10.610 --> 16:12.320
We'll defeat the Citroid for sure.

16:12.950 --> 16:14.420
The Citroid taught me that...

16:15.550 --> 16:18.200
Pokémon have endless potential.

16:18.950 --> 16:20.260
Drawing out their strengths...

16:20.760 --> 16:22.420
...is a Trainer's duty.

16:24.490 --> 16:25.750
We believed in those words...

16:26.370 --> 16:27.730
...and worked hard.

16:28.500 --> 16:29.050
I made you...?

16:29.660 --> 16:30.210
Karakara,

16:30.490 --> 16:31.530
Bonemerang!

16:33.760 --> 16:35.200
Use Focus Blast once more!

16:44.060 --> 16:46.650
Elezard is unable to battle! Karakara wins!

16:47.190 --> 16:49.590
Therefore, the winner is challenger Alba!

16:50.070 --> 16:50.650
All right!

16:51.540 --> 16:52.470
We did it!

16:53.350 --> 16:55.060
Great job, Karakara!

16:55.910 --> 16:56.750
Thank you!

17:01.280 --> 17:03.350
Pokémon battles are nice.

17:04.480 --> 17:06.030
It was very fun.

17:06.710 --> 17:07.030
Yes.

17:10.550 --> 17:11.370
Here, take this.

17:11.980 --> 17:13.300
Congratulations.

17:13.820 --> 17:15.200
This is the Voltage Badge.

17:16.890 --> 17:17.990
Thank you so much.

17:21.710 --> 17:22.980
Isn't that great, Alba?

17:22.980 --> 17:23.430
Yes!

17:23.890 --> 17:25.640
Citroid, you battled well too!

17:25.870 --> 17:29.340
Coil, Rarecoil and Elezard all did <i>their</i> best, too!

17:29.570 --> 17:29.810
Yes!

17:30.390 --> 17:32.170
Thank you for the support.

17:33.380 --> 17:35.770
I want to bring out my Pokémon's strengths much further.

17:36.400 --> 17:38.820
I want to know a lot more about Pokémon.

17:39.320 --> 17:41.490
Please teach me, Citron-sama.

17:45.330 --> 17:45.850
Of course!

17:46.720 --> 17:48.140
Let us grow together.

17:50.150 --> 17:50.530
Okay!

17:54.100 --> 17:54.750
All right,

17:55.210 --> 17:59.210
now that you're all gathered together again, it's time for the Kalos League award ceremony.

17:59.770 --> 18:00.620
Award ceremony?

18:01.170 --> 18:02.240
Oh, right.

18:02.820 --> 18:05.470
It was interrupted because of the trouble with the Flare Gang.

18:06.070 --> 18:06.900
I see.

18:07.310 --> 18:09.130
So this is where you and Alan will...

18:09.550 --> 18:11.830
In that case, let's award everyone!

18:12.100 --> 18:12.770
Everyone?

18:13.390 --> 18:16.220
After all, we all fought really hard against the Flare Gang, right?

18:16.710 --> 18:17.220
So that's why...

18:18.320 --> 18:19.850
Of course. That's what I had planned.

18:25.400 --> 18:28.850
Glory to you Trainers, as well as your Pokémon.

18:29.450 --> 18:31.000
Congratulations on coming in second place at the Kalos League.

18:31.910 --> 18:33.000
Thank you very much.

18:36.390 --> 18:37.010
Congratulations.

18:38.600 --> 18:39.000
Alan,

18:39.480 --> 18:39.890
what do you think?

18:40.450 --> 18:42.860
Wanna help me with my research again?

18:44.630 --> 18:45.280
I...

18:45.430 --> 18:46.640
I'm lacking aides.

18:47.190 --> 18:48.720
And considering the state Miare is in...

18:49.240 --> 18:50.150
I need you.

18:54.290 --> 18:54.650
Okay.

18:55.650 --> 18:57.030
I'm so glad for you, Alan!

19:15.150 --> 19:15.680
10!

19:16.250 --> 19:16.510
9!

19:17.380 --> 19:17.860
8!

19:18.470 --> 19:18.850
7!

19:19.560 --> 19:20.290
6!

19:20.670 --> 19:21.560
5!

19:21.800 --> 19:24.110
Today's a very joyous day.

19:21.850 --> 19:22.550
4!

19:22.870 --> 19:23.430
3!

19:24.010 --> 19:24.710
2!

19:24.430 --> 19:25.660
Gotta make this one flashy.

19:25.130 --> 19:25.830
1!

19:26.350 --> 19:28.500
0!

19:36.470 --> 19:37.400
So pretty!

19:37.400 --> 19:38.840
Electricity is incredible!

19:38.840 --> 19:40.310
Eureka is so excited!

19:40.310 --> 19:42.440
It is the light indicating the Miare Gym's revival.

19:42.770 --> 19:45.670
I'll shine just as brightly as the Prism Tower here.

19:46.240 --> 19:47.240
Let's do this, Pikachu!

19:48.790 --> 19:49.610
Me too!

19:50.810 --> 19:53.710
By the way, Serena, what are you going to do next?

19:55.140 --> 19:56.470
I'm a bit torn, you see.

19:58.910 --> 20:00.350
Will you come with me?

20:03.880 --> 20:05.130
You'll be fine, Serena.

20:06.530 --> 20:07.810
I believe in you.

20:10.070 --> 20:10.400
Yeah.

20:11.060 --> 20:11.720
Thank you!

20:14.220 --> 20:19.970
Under the dazzling light of the Prism Tower, Satoshi and his friends each pledge new decisions.

20:20.690 --> 20:24.070
And so, their journey continues on.

21:47.300 --> 21:50.500
Advance info on the new series, "Sun & Moon"!

21:50.570 --> 21:53.270
I've never been in a Pokémon taxi before!

21:50.990 --> 21:54.530
The start of a new adventure

21:51.750 --> 21:54.530
The setting of Satoshi and Pikachu's new adventure is...

21:54.820 --> 21:57.240
The Alola Region

21:55.520 --> 21:56.950
...the Alola region!

21:57.490 --> 22:04.330
Pokémon and people help each other

21:58.020 --> 21:59.580
The islands are abundant with nature...

21:59.780 --> 22:02.960
...and Pokémon and people live together and help each other out!

22:04.500 --> 22:09.210
RIDE POKÉMON

22:05.130 --> 22:09.210
One part of the Alola region's culture is Ride Pokémon.

22:09.380 --> 22:12.800
KENTAUROS
Land Ride Pokémon

22:10.380 --> 22:12.290
Even places humans cannot reach on their own...

22:12.480 --> 22:15.960
...can be accessed with the help of Pokémon!

22:12.970 --> 22:15.260
LIZARDON
Sky Ride Pokémon

22:15.430 --> 22:18.790
SAMEHADER
Sea Ride Pokémon

22:18.930 --> 22:20.610
NYABBY

22:19.590 --> 22:23.970
Also, lots of new Pokémon that you've never seen before will appear!

22:20.810 --> 22:22.640
NAMAKOBUSHI

22:22.770 --> 22:24.600
KITERUGUMA

22:24.770 --> 22:27.020
AGOJIMUSHI

22:24.890 --> 22:26.610
What's this Pokémon called?

22:27.190 --> 22:31.530
NASSY
(Alola Form)

22:27.910 --> 22:31.080
There are also Pokémon with forms exclusive to the Alola region!

22:31.650 --> 22:33.610
ASHIMARI

22:32.610 --> 22:35.160
Now, what kind of encounters await?

22:33.780 --> 22:35.620
KAPU-KOKEKO

22:35.620 --> 22:37.190
All right, let's race, Pikachu!

22:35.620 --> 22:41.870
Starts in November

22:36.240 --> 22:40.380
The new series, "Pocket Monsters Sun & Moon", will start in November!

22:40.560 --> 22:41.340
Look forward to it!

22:41.870 --> 22:46.880
Sunday October 9th at 8am!

22:42.960 --> 22:44.420
A transformation into Kabigon!

22:44.390 --> 22:45.970
All right, here comes Koike Nyarth!

22:44.870 --> 22:45.950
On Sunday at 8am!

22:49.010 --> 22:50.910
All right, everyone! Let's go together!

22:51.130 --> 22:52.210
Towards our next adventure!

22:53.700 --> 22:56.080
I made a promise to Yashio-san... I need to give her an answer.

22:56.690 --> 22:57.750
But I don't know how to answer yet...

22:58.530 --> 22:59.680
Why don't you battle me?

23:00.040 --> 23:00.180
Huh?

23:00.860 --> 23:05.530
You see... When I'm gloomy because of something, battling with my Pokémon helps me clear my head.

23:06.050 --> 23:06.780
Satoshi...

23:07.600 --> 23:10.070
Next time on Pocket Monsters XY&Z:

23:10.420 --> 23:13.650
One Last Battle with Satoshi! Serena's Choice!!

23:13.280 --> 23:16.770
Next Time

23:13.280 --> 23:16.770
One Last Battle with Satoshi!
Serena's Choice!!

23:14.230 --> 23:16.150
Everyone, get Pokémon!

23:16.810 --> 23:26.860
Next episode:

23:16.810 --> 23:21.790
A performance in Miare City!

23:17.670 --> 23:22.240
Pocket Monsters XY&Z was brought to you by these sponsors.

23:21.820 --> 23:26.860
What is Serena's decision...!?
